# Line endings, decided once and applied everywhere.
#
# Without this, each machine's core.autocrlf setting decides for itself. On
# Windows that means Git rewrites every file to CRLF on checkout and warns about
# it on every commit, while the Linux box that actually builds the image checks
# out LF. Same repository, two different working trees.
#
# LF is the right answer here: the Docker build, nginx and every shell script
# run on Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or the shebang line breaks inside the container.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files are never converted — doing so corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
